{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויכל אלהים", :translit "va-yekhel elohim", :gloss "and Elohim finished"} {:he "וחמד", :translit "va-hamad", :gloss "and He desired"} {:he "חמדת ימים אותו קראת", :translit "hamdat yamim oto karat", :gloss "the desire of days, You called it"} {:he "ויכלו", :translit "va-yekhulu", :gloss "and they were finished"} {:he "מלאכתו", :translit "mela'ekhto", :gloss "His work"} {:he "שמים וארץ וים", :translit "shamayim va-eretz va-yam", :gloss "heaven and earth and sea"} {:he "ואין כתיב ויהי ערב ויהי בוקר יום השביעי", :translit "ve-ein katuv va-yehi erev va-yehi boker yom ha-shevi'i", :gloss "and it is not written 'and it was evening and it was morning, the seventh day'"} {:he "מוסיפין מחול על הקודש", :translit "mosifin me-hol al ha-kodesh", :gloss "we add from the profane onto the sacred"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מלאכתו" "מלאכתו" "מלאכתו"]}], :frame {:text "Targum Yerushalmi renders 'va-yekhel' as 'va-hamad,' linking to the phrase 'hamdat yamim oto karat' applied to Shabbat. The word 'mela'ekhto' appears three times in Genesis 2:2, corresponding to three realms of creation — heaven, earth, and sea — from which God rested. The closing formula 'and it was evening and it was morning, the seventh day' is absent from the verse; Rashi (Genesis 2:2, citing Bereshit Rabbah) explains this is because God added from profane time onto the sacred, entering Shabbat earlier than the literal sixth day's end.", :sources ["Targum Yerushalmi Genesis 2:2" "Rashi Genesis 2:2" "Bereshit Rabbah"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וישבות", :translit "va-yishbot", :gloss "and He rested"} {:he "ואידך וישבות המן", :translit "ve-idakh va-yishbot ha-man", :gloss "and the other 'va-yishbot ha-man'"} {:he "הוא אשר דיבר ה' שבתון שבת קודש", :translit "hu asher diber Hashem shabbaton shabbat kodesh", :gloss "it is that which Hashem spoke, a sabbath observance, a holy sabbath"} {:he "וישבות ביום השביעי", :translit "va-yishbot be-yom ha-shevi'i", :gloss "and He rested on the seventh day"} {:he "וישבות המן", :translit "va-yishbot ha-man", :gloss "and the manna rested"} {:he "שהמן פסק מלירד בשבת", :translit "she-haman pasak me-la-redet ba-shabbat", :gloss "that the manna ceased descending on Shabbat"} {:he "ברכו במן וקדשו במן", :translit "berekhu be-man u-kideshu be-man", :gloss "they blessed with the manna and sanctified with the manna"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וישבות" "ושבת"]}], :frame {:text "The word 'va-yishbot' appears twice in the Masorah: in Genesis 2:2 and in Exodus 16:30 ('va-yishbot ha-man'). This pairing hints that the command of Shabbat given with the manna (Exodus 16:25) was already embedded in the creation narrative. Shabbat as observed in the wilderness — the manna ceasing on the seventh day — is the subject of Kiddushin (38a), which proves the manna fell for six days and ceased on the seventh. A further midrashic reading of the shared root interprets that Israel blessed with the manna and sanctified with the manna, connecting the language of resting to acts of blessing and sanctification surrounding Shabbat.", :sources ["Exodus 16:25" "Exodus 16:30" "Kiddushin 38a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["מלאכתו" "מלאכתו" "מלאכתו"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מלאכתו", :refs ["Genesis 2:2" "Genesis 2:3" "Genesis 39:11" "1 Kings 7:14" "Nehemiah 4:9" "2 Chronicles 16:5"], :n 6, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מלאכתו", :refs ["Genesis 2:2" "Genesis 2:3" "Genesis 39:11" "1 Kings 7:14" "Nehemiah 4:9" "2 Chronicles 16:5"], :n 6, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מלאכתו", :refs ["Genesis 2:2" "Genesis 2:3" "Genesis 39:11" "1 Kings 7:14" "Nehemiah 4:9" "2 Chronicles 16:5"], :n 6, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וישבות" "ושבת"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וישבות", :refs ["Genesis 2:2" "Genesis 2:3" "Genesis 8:22" "Genesis 27:44" "Genesis 28:21" "Genesis 42:38" "Genesis 44:29" "Genesis 44:31"], :n 150, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "ושבת", :refs ["Deuteronomy 4:30" "Deuteronomy 23:14" "Deuteronomy 30:2" "Isaiah 1:13" "Ezekiel 46:17" "Lamentations 2:6"], :n 6, :lens :exact}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:04:11.795929912Z", :model "glm-5.2"}